# Passwordless sudo for the container user (developer).
#
# Deliberately broad: these flavors exist so agents and users can elevate
# inside the rootless container, including for apt packages, system users, and
# service management under the container's own limits. The launch side is the
# real boundary: sudo images are started without --security-opt no-new-privileges
# (the Makefile derives that flag from the FLAVOR), and the rootless container
# is what keeps host access bounded.
#
# Fine-grained rules were rejected on purpose. A sudoers file that grants every
# command except something is a maze agents will trip over, and the real
# boundary is outside the container: never run a sudo image with a sensitive
# host mount or a podman socket mounted into it.
developer ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
